<name>Engine</name>
<section id="10006_S000J" variety="S000J">
<name>Engine Control</name>
<ttl id="10006_S000J_744E7_T004T" variety="T004T">
<name>EFI System (2AZ-FE)</name>
<para id="RM000003B8800DX" category="C" type-id="800K5" name-id="ESJK4-05" from="200912">
<dtccode>U0129/A2</dtccode>
<dtcname>Brake ECU Communication Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000003B8800DX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000I4L00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>CAN (Controller Area Network) is a serial data communication system for real-time applications. It is a multiplex communication system for vehicles, with a high communication speed (500kbps) and a malfunction detection function. By combining the CANH bus line and the CANL bus line, CAN performs communication based on differential voltage.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC NO.</ptxt>
<ptxt>SAE/TCCS</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Diagnosis Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Abnormal Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Malfunction Duration</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Others</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>U0129/A2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Lost communication between engine control computer and skid control computer</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>2.34 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
